<title>RUSSIA: TENNIS-ST PETERSBURG OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-ST PETERSBURG OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG, Russia 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the</p>
<p>$300,000 St Petersburg Open men's tennis tournament (prefix</p>
<p>number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Played Tuesday:</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>1-Michael Stich (Germany) beat Richard Fromberg (Australia) 4-6</p>
<p>7-5 7-6 (9-7)</p>
<p>4-Daniel Vacek (Czech) beat Patrik Fredriksson (Sweden) 6-4 3-6</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>Stephane Simian (France) beat Igor Chelychev (Russia)</p>
<p>6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Fabrice Santoro (France) beat 6-Karol Kucera (Slovakia) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Magnus Norman (Sweden) beat Joost Winnink (Netherlands) 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>3-David Prinosil (Germany) beat Lars Rehmann (Germany) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>7-Renzo Furlan (Italy) beat Lars Burgsmuller (Germany) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-2) 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>Orlin Stanoytchev (Bulgaria) beat Gianlucca Pozzi (Italy) 6-3</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Arnaud Clement (France) beat Andrei Olkhovsky (Russia) 7-5 4-1</p>
<p>(Olkhovsky retired injured)</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>Arnaud Clement (France) beat Greg Rusedski (Britain), walkover</p>
<p>(Rusedski injured)</p>
<p>Played Wednesday:</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>5-Thomas Johansson (Sweden) beat Alexander Volkov (Russia) 6-4 6-1</p>
<p>8-Kenneth Carlsen (Denmark) beat Francisco Roig (Spain) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Olivier Delaitre (France) beat Andrei Cherkasov (Russia) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>7-Renzo Furlan (Italy) beat Orlin Stanoytchev (Bulgaria) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Magnus Norman (Sweden) beat 3-David Prinosil (Germany) 1-6 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Jan Kroslak (Slovakia) beat Fabrice Santoro (France) 3-6 6-4 6-3</p>
</text>
